From 7b192917e8facd19d18bf914e47339a67e96cce4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shibco <cade@parare.al>
Date: Wed, 12 Aug 2026 15:42:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] winex11: bound and isolate pointer gesture output

Suppress ordinary wheel delivery while any button is held, including core and
XInput2 paths.

Middle-drag navigation is the only exception. It requires exactly its withheld
middle button and stops after any other button transition.

Keep delayed wheel input at its original window and point, and discard it after
an intervening button transition.

Bound direct movement, delayed-frame output, packet size, total travel, and the
number of coast messages. Reset history at discontinuities and process-wide
input boundaries so ignored or stale movement cannot reappear later.
